1879
01:12:48.220 --> 01:12:50.340
State the hypothesis with a direction.

1880
01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:52.000
Name the unit of analysis.

1881
01:12:52.400 --> 01:12:54.860
Give an operational definition for X and for Y,

1882
01:12:54.860 --> 01:12:57.540
and defend each one against a validity objection.

1883
01:12:57.820 --> 01:12:59.180
Say how you would assign X,

1884
01:12:59.340 --> 01:13:02.440
or how you would approximate assignment if you cannot randomize.

1885
01:13:02.640 --> 01:13:05.540
Name your control group and explain what makes it a credible

1886
01:13:05.540 --> 01:13:05.860
counterfactual.

1887
01:13:06.620 --> 01:13:09.800
Then admit the biggest threat to internal validity that remains.

1888
01:13:10.020 --> 01:13:11.120
That last move,

1889
01:13:11.280 --> 01:13:12.740
admitting the remaining weakness,

1890
01:13:13.020 --> 01:13:15.460
is what separates a B answer from an A answer.

1891
01:13:15.820 --> 01:13:16.680
Frame 3.

1892
01:13:16.960 --> 01:13:18.380
Why is this measure bad?

